<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Weak retail sales hit CNA Gallo earnings.</title>
<headline>Weak retail sales hit CNA Gallo earnings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline			 24.1	   vs 25.8</p>
<p>    - net				24.6	   vs 25.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			  10.5	   vs 10.5</p>
<p>    Net income			 86.8	   vs 89.2</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			   102.4	   vs 115.4</p>
<p>    Tax				  22.1	   vs 37.8</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    0.58	   vs 3.33</p>
<p>    Turnover			  1,610	   vs 1,459</p>
<p>    Exceptional charge		7.3	   vs 3.4</p>
<p>    Share of associates'	    9.8	   vs 14.4</p>
<p>Full name: CNA Gallo Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company sales in the second half been disappointing, hitting final earnings, due to pressure on consumers.</p>
<p>A spate of strategic acquisitions and new business initiatives by the South African retailer and leisure firm contributed 88 million rand to the group's turnover and 4.7 million rand to headline earnings for the year under review.</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast headline EPS of 25.3, with the range 24.5-26.8, and a dividend of 10.7, with the range 10.5-11.1.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
